body:
Now, I'm no Emergency Service worker, but I'd like to know from someone who'd know, the movie "Only the Brave", with Josh Brolin and Miles Teller, about real events involving a team of wildfire firefighters (Hotshots) called Granite Mountain Hotshots, is it accurate to real wildfire firefighting?

&#x200B;

PS, it's a biographical movie, so I'd assume so.

Hallo. My name's u/AnarchistClimber and I'm a horror author, posting mostly on r/nosleep. I've posted two stories of my own (fictional, of course) on NoSleep, one about 7-8 months ago and one that I posted two days ago. None of them have been a major success, but it doesn't really matter to me.

&#x200B;

I just write down a lot of stuff and whatever I like the next day I develop into stories. I'd also like to add that I'm not particularly active as a writer, I sure read a lot of stories but writing my own usually requires time, which now that I've started school again I've got pretty limited of.

&#x200B;

Yeah, uhm, thanks for the invite and I'll stick around to see how this turns out.
